    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0231",
      "sequence": 243,
      "meaning": "‘Dear one, this is Janaka’s daughter, for whom the bow-sacrifice is being held. Her friends have brought her to worship Gaurī, and she moves through the garden spreading radiance. Beholding her unearthly beauty has stirred my naturally pure mind. Providence knows the entire cause; hear, brother, my limbs throb auspiciously. It is the Raghu line’s inborn nature that no one sets foot on an evil path. I have absolute trust in my mind, which has never looked at another’s wife even in a dream. Rare in the world are those excellent men whose enemies never see their backs in battle, whose eyes and minds never seek another’s wife, and whose hands never refuse a petitioner.’ While he spoke with his brother, his mind remained attracted by Sītā’s form, drinking like a bee the nectarous beauty of her lotus face.",
