    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0233",
      "sequence": 245,
      "meaning": "The two heroes, handsome limits of beauty, had bodies like blue and yellow lotuses. Peacock feathers shone finely on their heads, with clusters and flower buds between them. A forehead-mark and beads of perspiration were lovely; ornaments cast splendor over their handsome ears. Their arched brows and curling hair were striking, their fresh-lotus eyes tinged red. Graceful chin, nose and cheeks, and their playfully smiling faces bought the mind outright. I cannot describe the beauty of those faces, which would shame countless Loves. Jewel necklaces rested on their chests and their fine conch-like necks rose above; their arms had the strength of young elephants and formed the boundary of Love’s art. The dark prince held a leaf-cup of flowers in his left hand; ‘Friend, how exceedingly charming he is!’ With a lion’s waist, yellow cloth, and a treasury of beauty and character, the ornaments of the solar line made the companions forget themselves.",
