    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0234",
      "sequence": 246,
      "meaning": "One discerning friend regained composure, took Sītā’s hand and said, ‘Meditate on Gaurī again later; why not first look fully at the royal youths?’ Sītā shyly opened her eyes and beheld the two lions of Raghu before her. Looking from Rāma’s nails to his crown, she remembered her father’s vow and became deeply distressed. When the companions saw her helpless, a grave unease arose and they all spoke anxiously. ‘We shall come again tomorrow at this very time,’ one friend said, smiling inwardly. Hearing the veiled remark, Sītā blushed, then feared her mother because she had delayed. With great fortitude she brought Rāma into her heart, but again recognized that her own fate lay under her father’s authority. On the pretext of looking at deer, birds and trees, she turned back repeatedly; gazing again and again at Raghubīra’s beauty, her love grew far from little.",
